   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 509 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto authorizing the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Port\nChester, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8041",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8041-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 509 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8041\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 509 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the imposition of an occupancy tax in the\nvillage of Port Chester, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize the Village of Port Chester to extend a room occupancy tax\nnot to exceed 3%.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill extends the current Village of Port Chester occupancy tax for\nanother three years until December 31, 2025.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nn/a\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends the current Village of Port Chester occupancy tax.\nThe Village of Port Chester anticipates using this revenue as an alter-\nnative to raising property taxes or additional borrowing.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: Chap. 709\n\n2016: Chap. 509\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State of New York.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
